Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||06-25-2001||12:29 PM||||Did you know the GT wheels are polished on the back inside rim also ?  Just like the front outer rim is polished<P>I took my wheels off, to do some clean up & to check the brakes.<P>When I first looked at the backside, they were filthy dirty & all black.  I washed them up, and the black "gook" started to come off.<P>I won't fool you, it took some time to get through all of it, but it's there !!<P>They look great now, the shine is visible looking through the "lace" of the wheel.<BR> (this photo was taken before)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_wheel.jpg">     <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||CoolBlue87GT||06-25-2001||07:24 PM||||<BR>I guess everyone knew, judging by the many replies  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Where is everybody ?||||reg||9
Z||000002||btoth||06-25-2001||07:47 PM||||I didn't know that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||06-25-2001||08:29 PM||||Once a year, I take off the wheels and clean the insides. A PITA job.  Lots of tar/grease and brake dust removal chemicals required.||||reg||1
Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||06-25-2001||08:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>Lots of tar/grease and brake dust removal chemicals required.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I used this stuff called Goo Gone.  Worked really good. Especially on the undercoating overspray. <P>If I could meet the guy that sprayed mine, I'd smack him. Looked all black when I started.||||reg||1
